.policy "prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction" revision 1
.description "Inside an interactive $transaction callback, query through tx and pass tx to helpers, not through the outer Prisma client, whose queries run outside the transaction."
.language typescript
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.ts", "**/*.mts", "**/*.cts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.js", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.mjs", "**/*.cjs"
.scope exclude "**/*.test.*", "**/*.spec.*", "**/*.cy.*", "**/__tests__/**", "**/test/**", "**/tests/**", "**/e2e/**"
.scope exclude "**/__mocks__/**", "**/*.stories.*", "**/*.story.*", "**/__stories__/**", "**/__fixtures__/**"
.scope exclude "**/fixtures/**", "**/node_modules/**", "**/dist/**", "**/build/**", "**/out/**", "**/.next/**"
.scope exclude "**/coverage/**", "**/vendor/**", "**/.venv/**", "**/.yarn/**", "**/generated/**", "**/__generated__/**"
.scope exclude "**/*.generated.*", "**/*.gen.*", "**/*.min.js", "**/*.d.ts"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. An interactive transaction, `<client>.$transaction(async (tx) => …)`, runs its
// queries on one connection, through `tx`. A query made inside the callback through the outer client goes out on
// another pooled connection, outside the transaction: a write commits even when the callback throws and the
// transaction rolls back (an order marked paid with its line items gone), a read misses the transaction's own
// uncommitted writes, and a write to a row the transaction has locked waits for it until the transaction times out
// (P2028). Prisma's issue #17215 calls the helper form easy to write and hard to catch in review. Prisma 5 to 7;
// Prisma 8's `db.transaction(async (tx) => …)` and `tx.orm.<schema>.<Model>` are not matched yet.
// Reported, inside the body of a function written inline as the first argument of `<r>.$transaction(…)`, or in a
// callback an array method there runs at once (`ids.map((id) => …)`, forEach, flatMap, filter, reduce, some, every,
// find):
//   - a query through the same client r: `r.<model>.<op>(…)` (findMany … groupBy and their OrThrow forms),
//     `r.$queryRaw` / `$executeRaw` (tagged or Unsafe), `r.$runCommandRaw(…)`, and a nested `r.$transaction(…)`,
//     which is a transaction of its own. r is the same binding (`prisma`, an import), the same chain of the same
//     binding (`ctx.db`, `this.prisma`), or, through an import, the same exported client (a default export of the
//     client counts as the client).
//   - a call `g(…)` of a function g of the project (same file, or imported, one hop) whose body queries that same
//     client by its module binding, when the call passes nothing that names the callback's parameters.
//   - the same with a callback that takes no parameter: every query in it then runs outside the transaction.
// Left alone:
//   - `tx.<model>.<op>(…)`, and a helper given `tx` (`auditWith(tx, …)`, `recordEvent("x", tx)`, `g({ tx })`).
//   - a callback whose parameter shadows the client's name (`async (prisma) => prisma.order.update(…)`).
//   - another client (a second database's `analytics.event.create(…)`): its writes were never in the transaction.
//   - the array form `prisma.$transaction([prisma.a.create(…), …])`: its queries are the transaction's.
//   - queries before or after the `$transaction` call, and in its catch.
//   - queries in a function the callback only defines, to run later: `after(async () => …)`,
//     `onCommit.push(() => …)`, a closure it returns. They run after the commit (on `tx` they would fail, P2028),
//     which is the deliberate out-of-transaction write. Other nested functions (`.then(…)`, event handlers) are not
//     followed either, a gap (below).
//   - a helper whose query goes through a parameter, defaulted to the client or not (`client = prisma`).
//   - a callback that takes a Postgres advisory lock (`tx.$queryRaw\`SELECT pg_try_advisory_xact_lock(…)\``, also
//     pg_advisory_lock and the _shared forms): the transaction is a mutex that locks no row, and work on the outer
//     client under it is chosen to run outside it. `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` is no such mutex: it locks rows, which an
//     outer-client write to them then waits on.
// Gaps: a callback passed by name (`$transaction(work)`); helpers reached through a method (`this.svc.f()`), an
// object (`repo.f()`), two hops or more, or a default export of a function; a helper that defaults to the client
// and is called without `tx` (`recordEvent("x")`); the outer client passed to a helper (`f(prisma)`); a client from
// a workspace package the importer and the helper name by different specifiers (`@repo/db` and `./client`); a second
// client of the same database under another name (`db.$transaction(async (tx) => prisma.x.create(…))`); a query in a
// `.then(…)` callback of an awaited promise, or in a callback a wrapper runs at once (`withRetries(() => …)`), which
// do run inside the transaction; an alias (`@/x`, `~/x`) the tsconfig's `paths` do not map, which names the module
// by its specifier, as a package's import does. A helper whose body queries one client by two names (`db` and its
// default export) is reported once for each, at that name's first query.

#include "tsx/eslint-a-common.rerail"

.violation OuterClientInTransaction(at: node, call: symbol, r: symbol, l: number) "`{call}(…)` runs inside the interactive `{r}.$transaction(…)` callback at line {l} but goes through the outer client `{r}`, not the callback's transaction client: Prisma sends it on another pooled connection, outside the transaction, so a write commits even when the transaction rolls back, a read misses the transaction's uncommitted writes, and a write to a row the transaction has locked waits until the transaction times out (P2028). Call it on the transaction client the callback receives (`async (tx) => tx.<model>.<op>(…)`; add that parameter if the callback has none). If it must run outside the transaction on purpose (an audit or failure record that has to survive a rollback), make it after the `$transaction` call or in its catch instead."
OuterClientInTransaction(q, call, rt, l) :- gct_direct(q, c, r), docof(q, d), gct_doc(d), callee(q, m), text(m, call),
    text(r, rt), line(c, l).

.violation HelperUsesOuterClient(at: node, g: symbol, r: symbol, l: number, q: symbol, p: symbol, ql: number) "`{g}(…)`, called inside the interactive `{r}.$transaction(…)` callback at line {l}, queries the module's Prisma client itself (`{q}(…)` at {p}:{ql}) instead of a client it is given, so that query runs on another connection, outside this transaction: a write commits even when the transaction rolls back, and a read misses the transaction's uncommitted writes. Give `{g}` a client parameter (`client: Prisma.TransactionClient = prisma`), query through it, and pass the callback's `tx`. If `{g}` must write outside the transaction on purpose (an audit or failure record that has to survive a rollback), call it after the `$transaction` call or in its catch instead."
HelperUsesOuterClient(k, gx, rt, l, qt, p, ql) :- gct_local_first(k, c, r, gx, sb, ql, qt, p), gct_sym(r, sa),
    gct_canon(sa, s), gct_canon(sb, s), text(r, rt), line(c, l).
HelperUsesOuterClient(k, gx, rt, l, qt, p, ql) :- gct_import_call(k, c, r, g), gct_sym(r, sa), gct_canon(sa, s),
    gct_helper_first(g, s, gx, ql, qt, p), text(r, rt), line(c, l).
// gct_doc(d): d is a document of the run. Each finding reads it at its own document, declared across files:
// HelperUsesOuterClient reads other files' helpers (gct_helper_first), and the findings are written out together, so
// a finding read per file alone would hand its node to the cross-file part (decision 0677).
.decl gct_doc(d: number) cross_file
gct_doc(d) :- doc(d, _, _).

// gct_tx(c, r, f): call c is `<r>.$transaction(f, …)`, f a function written inline: the interactive form.
.decl gct_tx(c: node, r: node, f: node)
gct_tx(c, r, f) :- callee(c, m), kind(m, "member_expression"), field(m, "property", p), text(p, "$transaction"),
    field(m, "object", r0), deparen(r0, r), call_arg(c, a, 0), deparen(a, f),
    (kind(f, "arrow_function") ; kind(f, "function_expression")).
// gct_in_tx(n, c, r, f): call n runs while f, the callback of transaction call c on client r, runs: it is in f's own
// body, or in a callback an array method there calls at once (`ids.map((id) => …)`, also under `Promise.all`). A
// function the callback only defines runs later, after the commit or never inside it (`after(() => …)`,
// `onCommit.push(() => …)`, a returned closure), and is not followed: moving its query to `tx` would break it.
.decl gct_in_tx(n: node, c: node, r: node, f: node)
gct_in_tx(n, c, r, f) :- gct_tx(c, r, f), kind(n, "call_expression"), nearest(n, g, gct_fn), gct_runs(g, f).
.decl gct_fn(k: symbol)
gct_fn("arrow_function"). gct_fn("function_expression"). gct_fn("function_declaration").
gct_fn("method_definition"). gct_fn("generator_function"). gct_fn("generator_function_declaration").
// gct_runs(g, f): g's body runs while transaction callback f runs (the set side-effect-in-transaction uses).
.decl gct_runs(g: node, f: node)
gct_runs(f, f) :- gct_tx(_, _, f).
gct_runs(g, f) :- gct_runs(h, f), kind(k, "call_expression"), nearest(k, h, gct_fn), callee(k, m),
    static_prop(m, _, x), gct_iter(x), call_arg(k, a, 0), deparen(a, g),
    (kind(g, "arrow_function") ; kind(g, "function_expression")).
.decl gct_iter(x: symbol)
gct_iter("map"). gct_iter("forEach"). gct_iter("flatMap"). gct_iter("filter"). gct_iter("reduce").
gct_iter("some"). gct_iter("every"). gct_iter("find").

// gct_query(q, r): call q sends a query through client expression r: `r.<model>.<op>(…)` or `r.$queryRaw…`.
.decl gct_query(q: node, r: node)
gct_query(q, r) :- callee(q, m), kind(m, "member_expression"), field(m, "property", p), text(p, op), gct_op(op),
    field(m, "object", mo0), deparen(mo0, mo), kind(mo, "member_expression"), field(mo, "property", mp),
    kind(mp, "property_identifier"), text(mp, model), !prefix("$", model), field(mo, "object", r0), deparen(r0, r).
gct_query(q, r) :- callee(q, m), kind(m, "member_expression"), field(m, "property", p), text(p, x), gct_raw(x),
    field(m, "object", r0), deparen(r0, r).
.decl gct_op(op: symbol)
gct_op("findUnique"). gct_op("findUniqueOrThrow"). gct_op("findFirst"). gct_op("findFirstOrThrow").
gct_op("findMany"). gct_op("create"). gct_op("createMany"). gct_op("createManyAndReturn"). gct_op("update").
gct_op("updateMany"). gct_op("updateManyAndReturn"). gct_op("upsert"). gct_op("delete"). gct_op("deleteMany").
gct_op("count"). gct_op("aggregate"). gct_op("groupBy").
.decl gct_raw(x: symbol)
gct_raw("$queryRaw"). gct_raw("$executeRaw"). gct_raw("$queryRawUnsafe"). gct_raw("$executeRawUnsafe").
gct_raw("$queryRawTyped"). gct_raw("$runCommandRaw"). gct_raw("$transaction").

// gct_direct(q, c, r): query q, in the callback of transaction c, goes through r itself.
.decl gct_direct(q: node, c: node, r: node)
gct_direct(q, c, r) :- gct_in_tx(q, c, r, f), !gct_lock_tx(f), gct_query(q, r2), gct_same(r, r2).
// gct_lock_tx(f): callback f takes a Postgres advisory lock with a raw query: the transaction is a mutex.
.decl gct_lock_tx(f: node)
gct_lock_tx(f) :- gct_in_tx(q, _, _, f), callee(q, m), kind(m, "member_expression"), field(m, "property", p),
    text(p, x), gct_raw(x), x != "$transaction", field(q, "arguments", a), text(a, t),
    match("(?is).*\\bpg_(?:try_)?advisory_(?:xact_)?lock(?:_shared)?\\b.*", t).

// gct_same(r, r2): two client expressions of the same text whose root names the same thing: the same declaration,
// the same `this`, or (neither declared in the file) the same global name.
.decl gct_recv(r: node)
gct_recv(r) :- gct_tx(_, r, _).
gct_recv(r) :- gct_in_tx(q, _, _, _), gct_query(q, r).
.decl gct_chain(r: node, e: node)
gct_chain(r, r) :- gct_recv(r).
gct_chain(r, e2) :- gct_chain(r, e), kind(e, "member_expression"), field(e, "object", e0), deparen(e0, e2).
.decl gct_root(r: node, o: node)
gct_root(r, o) :- gct_chain(r, o), (kind(o, "identifier") ; kind(o, "this")).
.decl gct_same(r: node, r2: node)
gct_same(r, r2) :- gct_tx(_, r, _), gct_recv(r2), text(r, t), text(r2, t), gct_root(r, o), gct_root(r2, o2),
    gct_same_root(o, o2).
.decl gct_same_root(o: node, o2: node)
gct_same_root(o, o2) :- gct_root(_, o), gct_root(_, o2), ref_site(o, s), ref_site(o2, s).
gct_same_root(o, o2) :- gct_root(_, o), gct_root(_, o2), kind(o, "this"), kind(o2, "this"), this_owner(o, s),
    this_owner(o2, s).
gct_same_root(o, o2) :- gct_root(_, o), gct_root(_, o2), kind(o, "identifier"), kind(o2, "identifier"),
    !ref_site(o, _), !ref_site(o2, _), text(o, x), text(o2, x), docof(o, d), docof(o2, d).

// gct_call(k, c, r, n): call k, of the function the identifier n names, is in the callback of transaction c on the
// client identifier r, takes no advisory lock, and passes none of the callback's parameters.
.decl gct_call(k: node, c: node, r: node, n: node)
gct_call(k, c, r, n) :- gct_in_tx(k, c, r, f), !gct_lock_tx(f), callee(k, n), kind(n, "identifier"),
    kind(r, "identifier"), !gct_passes_param(k, f).
// gct_passes_param(k, f): an argument of call k names a parameter of f: `g(tx)`, `g({ tx })`, `g(a, tx)`.
.decl gct_passes_param(k: node, f: node)
gct_passes_param(k, f) :- gct_in_tx(k, _, _, f), call_arg(k, a, _), (i = a ; within(i, a)), ref_site(i, s),
    decl_site(f, _, s, "param", "value").

// A helper declared in the call's own file, any function in reach, is read in that file.
// gct_local_query(k, c, r, g, q, sb): call k (gct_call) calls g, a function of its own file, whose body sends query q
// through a client identifier that names the binding sb (gct_sym).
.decl gct_local_query(k: node, c: node, r: node, g: node, q: node, sb: symbol)
gct_local_query(k, c, r, g, q, sb) :- gct_call(k, c, r, n), ref_site(n, s), gct_fn_site(s, g), field(g, "body", gb),
    within(q, gb), gct_query(q, r3), kind(r3, "identifier"), gct_sym(r3, sb).
// gct_local_first(k, c, r, gx, sb, ql, qt, p): of those queries through sb, the first is `qt(…)` at line ql of the file
// at path p; the helper is named gx.
.decl gct_local_first(k: node, c: node, r: node, gx: symbol, sb: symbol, ql: number, qt: symbol, p: symbol)
gct_local_first(k, c, r, gx, sb, ql, qt, p) :- gct_local_query(k, c, r, g, _, sb), gct_fn_name(g, gx),
    ql = min m : { gct_local_query(k, c, r, g, q0, sb), line(q0, m) }, gct_local_query(k, c, r, g, q2, sb),
    line(q2, ql), callee(q2, m2), text(m2, qt), docof(q2, d), doc(d, p, _).

// An imported helper is another file's: each file states its top-level functions' queries by symbol, path and line
// (gct_helper_query), and the call reads them by the helper's symbol (gct_helper_first, across files).
// gct_import_call(k, c, r, g): call k (gct_call) calls the imported binding g ("module#name").
.decl gct_import_call(k: node, c: node, r: node, g: symbol)
gct_import_call(k, c, r, g) :- gct_call(k, c, r, n), ref_site(n, sp), import_binding(sp, _, _, _), gct_sym(n, g).
// gct_helper_query(g, gx, sb, l, qt, p): the top-level function g ("module#name"), named gx, of the file at path p,
// sends a query `qt(…)` at line l through a client identifier that names the binding sb.
.decl gct_helper_query(g: symbol, gx: symbol, sb: symbol, l: number, qt: symbol, p: symbol)
gct_helper_query(@qname(m, gx), gx, sb, l, qt, p) :- gct_fn_site(s, g), top_level(s, gx), field(g, "body", gb),
    within(q, gb), gct_query(q, r3), kind(r3, "identifier"), gct_sym(r3, sb), line(q, l), callee(q, m2),
    text(m2, qt), docof(s, d), ts_module(d, m), doc(d, p, _).
// gct_helper_first(g, s, gx, ql, qt, p): of helper g's queries through the client s (gct_canon), the first.
.decl gct_helper_first(g: symbol, s: symbol, gx: symbol, ql: number, qt: symbol, p: symbol) cross_file
gct_helper_first(g, s, gx, ql, qt, p) :- gct_helper_query(g, gx, sb, _, _, _), gct_canon(sb, s),
    ql = min l : { gct_helper_query(g, _, sb0, l, _, _), gct_canon(sb0, s) }, gct_helper_query(g, gx, sb2, ql, qt, p),
    gct_canon(sb2, s).

.decl gct_callee(n: node)
gct_callee(n) :- gct_in_tx(k, _, _, _), callee(k, n), kind(n, "identifier").
.decl gct_fn_site(s: node, g: node)
gct_fn_site(g, g) :- kind(g, "function_declaration").
gct_fn_site(s, g) :- kind(s, "variable_declarator"), field(s, "value", v), deparen(v, g),
    (kind(g, "arrow_function") ; kind(g, "function_expression")).
.decl gct_fn_name(g: node, x: symbol)
gct_fn_name(g, x) :- gct_fn_site(s, g), (field(s, "name", n) ; s = g, field(g, "name", n)), text(n, x).

// gct_canon(s0, s): the client binding s0 is the client s: `export default prisma` makes "m#default" stand for
// "m#prisma"; any other binding is itself. The default export is the exporting file's, so this crosses, by symbols.
.decl gct_canon(s0: symbol, s: symbol) cross_file
gct_canon(s0, s) :- gct_client_name(s0), gct_default_of(s0, s).
gct_canon(s0, s0) :- gct_client_name(s0), !gct_default_of(s0, _).
.decl gct_client_name(s0: symbol)
gct_client_name(s0) :- gct_client_ask(r), gct_sym(r, s0).
.decl gct_client_ask(r: node)
gct_client_ask(r) :- gct_tx(_, r, _), kind(r, "identifier").
gct_client_ask(r) :- gct_query(q, r), kind(r, "identifier"), gct_fn_site(_, g), field(g, "body", gb), within(q, gb).
.decl gct_default_of(s0: symbol, s: symbol)
gct_default_of(@qname(m, "default"), @qname(m, x)) :- kind(e, "export_statement"), field(e, "value", v0),
    deparen(v0, v), kind(v, "identifier"), text(v, x), docof(e, d), ts_module(d, m).

// gct_sym(n, q): identifier n names the binding q ("module#name"): declared at the top of its file; imported from a
// module tsx/names resolves (a relative path, or an alias the tsconfig's `paths` map) and followed through
// `export … from` and `export *` (tsx_names__exports), or named "module#x" where that module exports no x it can
// follow (a `.ts` module seen from the `.tsx` run is only text there); or imported from a package, or by a specifier
// nothing resolves, which then names it ("@repo/db#prisma"), as tsx/names does for packages.
.decl gct_sym_ask(n: node)
gct_sym_ask(n) :- gct_callee(n).
gct_sym_ask(n) :- gct_client_ask(n).
.decl gct_sym(n: node, q: symbol)
gct_sym(n, @qname(m, x)) :- gct_sym_ask(n), ref_site(n, site), top_level(site, x), docof(n, d), ts_module(d, m).
gct_sym(n, q) :- gct_sym_ask(n), resolved_name(n, t, x), tsx_names__exports(t, x, q).
gct_sym(n, @qname(t, x)) :- gct_sym_ask(n), resolved_name(n, t, x), !tsx_names__exports(t, x, _).
gct_sym(n, @qname(s, x)) :- gct_sym_ask(n), ref_site(n, sp), import_binding(sp, _, s, x), x != "*", docof(n, d),
    !prefix(".", s), !target(d, s, _).

// The cases, `cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/`, read as one repository: each line ending in
// `// caught` is reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "package.json" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/package.json"
    .fixture "tsconfig.json" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/tsconfig.json"
    .fixture "src/lib/db.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/lib/db.ts"
    .fixture "src/lib/analytics-db.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/lib/analytics-db.ts"
    .fixture "src/lib/audit.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/lib/audit.ts"
    .fixture "src/lib/__tests__/orders.test.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/lib/__tests__/orders.test.ts"
    .fixture "src/app/orders/actions.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/app/orders/actions.ts"
    .fixture "src/app/orders/deferred.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/app/orders/deferred.ts"
    .fixture "src/server/billing/invoices.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/server/billing/invoices.ts"
    .fixture "src/server/billing/ledger.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/server/billing/ledger.ts"
    .fixture "src/server/jobs/migrate-plugins.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/server/jobs/migrate-plugins.ts"
    .fixture "src/server/api/routers/post.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/server/api/routers/post.ts"
    .fixture "src/server/db/index.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/server/db/index.ts"
    .fixture "src/server/billing/refunds.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/server/billing/refunds.ts"
    .fixture "src/server/jobs/stock.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/server/jobs/stock.ts"
    .fixture "src/server/jobs/sync.ts" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/server/jobs/sync.ts"
    .fixture "src/app/admin/orders/page.tsx" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/app/admin/orders/page.tsx"
    .fixture "src/app/admin/orders/close-button.tsx" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/app/admin/orders/close-button.tsx"
    .fixture "src/app/admin/orders/archive.tsx" from "../cases/prisma-practice-global-client-in-transaction/src/app/admin/orders/archive.tsx"
    .expect _ at "src/app/orders/actions.ts":10
    .expect _ at "src/app/orders/actions.ts":11
    .expect _ at "src/app/orders/deferred.ts":11
    .expect _ at "src/app/orders/deferred.ts":12
    .expect _ at "src/server/billing/invoices.ts":5
    .expect _ at "src/server/billing/invoices.ts":6
    .expect _ at "src/server/billing/invoices.ts":17
    .expect _ at "src/server/billing/ledger.ts":9
